      "signpost": "again",
      "definition": "added to a verb, or to a noun made from a verb, to make a word meaning do the action again",
      "explanation": "Use a hyphen when the word without one would look like a different word (*re-cover*, cover again; *recover*, get better), and often when **re-** comes before **e** (*re-enter*, also *reenter* in American English). In many common words such as **receive**, **report**, and **remember**, the letters *re* do not mean again.",
